Each `Store.DeleteMemo` invocation (parent + each direct comment) runs this full sequence; each resulting `DELETE FROM memo` can cascade-delete that memo’s `memo_share` rows.

---

## Tables **not** affected by `DeleteMemo`

| Table | Why excluded |
|-------|--------------|
| **`reaction`** | `ListReactions` at `memo_service.go:545-547` is read-only for webhook construction. No `DeleteReaction` anywhere in the delete path. Schema has no FK from `reaction` to `memo` (`content_id` is TEXT; `store/migration/sqlite/LATEST.sql:91-98`). |
| **`inbox`**, **`user`**, **`user_setting`**, **`system_setting`**, **`idp`**, **`user_identity`** | Not referenced in `DeleteMemo` or `Store.DeleteMemo`. |
| All others | No triggers on memo delete (triggers removed in migration `0.7`); current `LATEST.sql` defines no memo-delete triggers. |

---

## Summary

**Four tables** are touched when `DeleteMemo` runs:

1. **`memo`** — explicit delete (application code)
2. **`memo_relation`** — explicit delete (application code, two passes per memo)
3. **`attachment`** — explicit delete (application code, per linked attachment)
4. **`memo_share`** — implicit delete via `ON DELETE CASCADE` when `memo` rows are removed

Direct comment memos (`COMMENT` relations where `related_memo_id` = deleted memo) get the same treatment via recursive `Store.DeleteMemo` before the parent is deleted. **`reaction` rows are left in the database** after memo deletion.

